   "title": "Read me",
   "widgets_values": [
    "## Glitch shaped like a real thing\n\nSegment any picture, use the silhouette as the glitch's stencil. The generated image has nothing to do with the reference: only the **shape** of the damage comes from it.\n\n### Model\n\n`sam3.1_multiplex_fp16.safetensors` (1.75 GB) goes in `ComfyUI/models/checkpoints/`.\n\nhttps://huggingface.co/Comfy-Org/sam3.1/resolve/main/checkpoints/sam3.1_multiplex_fp16.safetensors\n\nIf the node is missing entirely, your ComfyUI predates SAM3. Swap in any other MASK source — the rest of the graph is unchanged.\n\n### Prompt syntax (it is not a weight)\n\nMax **32 tokens**. Commas separate categories, and `:N` is **how many objects** of that category to find, *not* a strength:\n\n```\ncat:2, window:4\n```\n\nParenthesised weights like `(cat:1.2)` are stripped — do not use them.\n\n### Leave `individual_masks` off\n\nOn, it returns one mask **per object**. The glitch node reads a stack of masks as *frames played across the sampling steps*, so five cats would animate over the run instead of glitching five regions.\n\n### Notes\n\n- The mask is stretched onto the image, so a reference at your output's aspect ratio keeps the silhouette undistorted.\n- The mask is a **soft multiplier**: grey = partial glitch. The blur in `Mask conditioning` is what feathers the edge. Nothing is thresholded.\n- Empty mask? Lower `threshold` toward 0.3, or use a simpler noun.\n- Needs comfyui-kjnodes for `GrowMaskWithBlur`."
   ]
  }
 ],
